DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ssttrrxxffrrmm() function transforms the _s_r_c string into a form such that
       the result of ssttrrccmmpp(3) on two strings that have been transformed  with
       ssttrrxxffrrmm()  is  the  same as the result of ssttrrccoollll(3) on the two strings
       before their transformation.  The first _s_i_z_e bytes of  the  transformed
       string  are  placed  in  _d_e_s_t.  The transformation is based on the pro‐
       gram’s current locale for category LLCC__CCOOLLLLAATTEE.  (See sseettllooccaallee(3)).

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       The ssttrrxxffrrmm() function returns the number of bytes  required  to  store
       the  transformed  string  in  _d_e_s_t  excluding the terminating null byte
       ('\0').  If the value returned is _s_i_z_e or more, the  contents  of  _d_e_s_t
       are indeterminate.

